Logic :

declare level globally
check whether root is null , then return 0
do like inorder traversal
go on left tree on recursion
when you come back increase the level by 1
chech whether the level is equal to k then return root value
then go on right recursive call
return the max value of left and right (this condition will return the root value if found , else 0)

Code :

class Solution {
    int lvl=0;
    public int kthSmallest(TreeNode root, int k) {
        if(root==null){
            return 0;
        }
       
        int val1=kthSmallest(root.left,k);
        lvl+=1;
        if(lvl==k){
            return root.val;
        }
        int val2=kthSmallest(root.right,k);
        return val1>val2?val1:val2;


    }
}
